00:01:05.539 --> 00:01:07.200
Chapter 4
In this chapter, the authors encourage readers

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.360
to “Embrace Difficulties” during learning.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.130
One example is the myth of errorless learning.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:18.970
Contrary to popular belief, making errors
during retrieval is a good thing for learning.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:19.970
In one experiment, students made errors while
studying, which improved their learning, yet

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:20.970
they didn't recognize this benefit.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:21.970
Huelser &amp; Metcalfe (2012)
Kang et al. (2011)

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:22.970
View fullsize
Make It Stick - 4 - Gadd.jpg

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:23.970
View fullsize
Make it Stick - 4 - Kemper.jpg

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:24.970
Chapter 5
Students need to “Avoid Illusions of Knowing.”

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:29.180
Students consistently predict higher test
performance following ineffective strategies

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:35.150
(e.g., re-reading) compared to more effective
strategies (e.g., retrieval practice).

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.150
Numerous studies reveal that students drop
flashcards too fast due to poor metacognition

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.150
and awareness of their own knowledge.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.150
Karpicke (2009)
Kornell &amp; Bjork (2008)

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:39.150
View fullsize

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.150
View fullsize
Make it Stick - 5 - Kemper.jpg

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:41.150
Chapter 6
Now is the time to “Get Beyond Learning

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.150
Styles.”

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:45.770
There is no empirical evidence that teaching
students consistent with their “learning

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:47.590
style” will improve learning.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:54.290
In contrast, methods supported by scientific
evidence – including retrieval – are robust

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:58.110
and reliable methods that improve student
learning in the classroom.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:01:59.540
Pashler et al. (2009)
Willingham et al. (2015)

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:00.540
